      "problem": "What is the infimum of the set $B=\\{-0.15,\\,-0.2,\\,0.05,\\,0,\\,9\\}?$\n\n$inf(B)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The infimum of a set $B$ is the greatest lower bound of $B.$\n\nIf $B$ is a finite set, the infimum of $B$ equals its minimum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}inf(B) & =min\\{-0.15,\\,-0.2,\\,0.05,\\,0,\\,9\\}=-0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
